(footprint "T68-6_Vertical_HandWound"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "manual")
	(generator_version "9.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "T68-6 iron powder toroid (Micrometals/Amidon mix 6, yellow, A_L = 4.7 nH/N^2 = 47 microH per 100 turns-squared -- catalogs typically list the latter form; use 4.7 in the N = sqrt(L_nH / A_L) formula), hand-wound, standing on edge with axis parallel to PCB. Top-down projection = rectangle OD (17.53 mm) x HT (4.83 mm). Two leads exit from opposite sides of the standing toroid: pad 1 above (north), pad 2 below (south), each offset slightly along the OD axis for the natural lead exit angle after 4-turn winding. Vertical mount reduces magnetic coupling to adjacent horizontal toroids. Anchor with nylon tie or hot glue after winding. For 20 m LPF (nominal 752 nH with 4 turns 22 AWG). Courtyard is tight: 0.2 mm beyond OD on the sides and 0.2 mm beyond pads on the lead-exit sides -- fine for hand assembly, allows packing right up against adjacent toroids. Rotate the footprint 90 deg on the PCB if you want the toroid axis along the signal direction (hole facing a neighboring flat toroid).")
	(tags "toroid iron powder t68-6 amidon micrometals hand wound vertical edge")
